[C1] PASS with gravity-work: face the energy row is minus the face work of the operator's own linearised mass flux: max |row - (-W^face)| = 7.1e-15 over 200 random rows
[C2] PASS on a Cartesian column both weights are 1/4 to round-off, and the Cartesian rows are the general rows with exactly 1/4 written in: max |weight - 1/4| = 6.1e-16 on a non-uniform column; max row difference 7.1e-15
[C3] PASS with gravity-work: cell the energy row keeps the cell work g m_i and adds only the dissipative |A| part of the face work: momentum entry of a: plain 9.80, with the |A| part 20.4983
[C4] PASS the projection work vanishes when the solve is applied exactly, and the clamp work keeps E + PE_d over a closed column: max |projection work| = 1.8e-14; sum V (W_clamp + phi dm) = 1.4e-17
